posts.text:
I asked Lebanon’s President Joseph Aoun for his message for the Israeli government and the Israeli people: “Aren’t you fed up with war since 1948? Do you really want to live in peace? Let’s sit and talk. For the Israeli government, it’s time for the power of reason to prevail over the reason of power.”

@LBpresidency

Video

After over four decades in the army, Lebanon’s President Joseph Aoun tells me, “I’ve been in combat situations many times. I was wounded twice. I’ve seen the hardship of war. That’s why I hate wars. That’s why I prefer negotiation… I don’t want my children, I don’t want the people, to live the same hardship.”

@LBpresidency

Video

“Entire families have been wiped out.” Lebanese President Joseph Aoun recounts the devastating toll of Israel’s war in his country against Hezbollah. “This is a 3-month-old baby,” he says, holding up a heartbreaking picture. “Is this an imminent threat?”

